in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @cascade
in @labeled
in @code/llvm
in @code/turing

# @cascade/code/llvm/turing — the LLVM IR → Turing tape ops cascade species.
#
# Path naming: per Alex 2026-06-23 directive — cascade species
# shards group by `@cascade/code/<source>/<target>`. Source
# language (LLVM IR) groups together at
# `shards/cascade/code/llvm/`; target (turing here; potentially
# other targets in future arcs) leafs at
# `shards/cascade/code/llvm/turing.mirror`.
#
# THIS species is Edge 2 of the concrete polyglot chain Alex
# ratified 2026-07-17 (verbatim, session-crystallizing):
#
#   *"So we can have @cascade/code/llvm/turing and
#    @cascade/code/rust/llvm. And boom. The loop closes."*
#
# The full chain per polyglot spec §4.1 (Mara `1ce68c3`,
# 2026-07-17):
#
#   Rust source
#     ↓  @cascade/code/rust/llvm      (sibling mint this tick)
#   LLVM IR
#     ↓  @cascade/code/llvm/turing    (THIS shard; LLVM IR →
#                                       abstract-machine tape ops)
#   Turing tape
#     ↓  @cascade/code/turing/mirror  (sibling mint this tick)
#   mirror substrate composition
#
# === substrate-already-had-the-word ===
#
# The LLVM IR → Turing tape mapping is well-known in translation-
# validation research (Alive2 / Lopes et al. 2021, cited per Mara
# `1ce68c3` §7). Each SSA instruction becomes a bounded tape-op
# sequence; each basic block becomes a state; each phi node
# becomes a branch. The substrate does NOT re-derive the mapping;
# THIS shard names the substrate-decl the FLOOR resolver (Reed
# Tick M3 domain) realizes.
#
# Church-Turing 1936 grounds the existence of the mapping (per
# Mara `1ce68c3` §7.2 proof sketch): every Turing-complete
# language admits a computable semantics-preserving translation
# to any universal machine model M. `@code/llvm` IS
# Turing-complete (LangRef §"Well-Formed IR"); `@code/turing`
# IS the abstract-machine tape model M; the cascade witnesses
# ONE such translation at substrate-decl altitude.
#
# === composition altitude: MACHINE-SUBSTRATE HUB ↔ FLOOR ===
#
# The source altitude is `@code/llvm` (landed
# `shards/code/llvm.mirror` this session; Mara M1 `62d1b1c`) —
# a MACHINE-SUBSTRATE HUB per polyglot spec §3.4. The target
# altitude is `@code/turing` (landed `shards/code/turing.mirror`
# this session; Mara M1 `7186410`) — the physical-substrate
# FLOOR per polyglot spec §2.3.
#
# This cascade is the crucial hub-to-floor edge: it grounds any
# language reaching @code/llvm (via a `@cascade/code/A/llvm`
# edge) in the substrate floor. Per polyglot spec §3.2
# composition axiom, THIS species composes with:
#
#   - `@cascade/code/rust/llvm` (sibling mint this tick) →
#     gives `@cascade/code/rust/turing` derived cascade.
#   - `@cascade/code/turing/mirror` (sibling mint this tick) →
#     gives `@cascade/code/llvm/mirror` derived cascade.
#   - Both above chained → gives the full Rust → mirror loop-
#     closing composition.
#
# === The cascade shape (LLVM IR → Turing tape ops) ===
#
# Source (LLVM IR admits per LangRef):
# - typed SSA values (register-typed; type system per LangRef
#   §"Type System")
# - basic blocks + terminators (structured control flow;
#   entry-block per function)
# - function signatures + attributes (calling conventions;
#   parameter attrs)
# - memory operations (load/store with alignment; alias info
#   via TBAA metadata)
# - vector instructions (SIMD; hardware-parallelism hints)
# - optimization opportunities (LLVM passes may reorder,
#   vectorize, inline, DCE)
# - register-level annotations (nsw, nuw, exact, arcp, etc.)
#
# Target (Turing tape preserves per Church-Turing 1936):
# - computation (SSA instructions → bounded tape-op sequences;
#   every LLVM op has a Turing-equivalent per
#   Turing-completeness of LLVM)
# - control flow (basic block → state; branches → state
#   transitions; phi nodes → state-conditional resolution)
# - reachability (transitive closure of state transitions
#   witnesses reachable configurations)
# - halt conditions (LLVM `ret`/`unreachable` → tape halt-state
#   per `@code/turing.program.halt_states`)
# - computational-equivalence (per Turing-completeness bijection
#   at the tape-model altitude)
#
# Per polyglot spec §4.4 Edge 2:
# - PRESERVED: control flow (branches → state transitions),
#   memory operations (read/write via tape), computation
#   (SSA → tape-ops).
# - LOST: register allocation, calling conventions, SIMD, type
#   information (tape is untyped bytes), platform ABI,
#   LLVM optimization opportunities (uniform tape ops preclude
#   backend-specific reordering), memory layout hints
#   (alignment, TBAA), register-level annotations (all become
#   uniform tape ops).
#
# The `loss_lens<@code/llvm, @code/turing>` measures these gaps
# against the LLVM LangRef source grammar + Church-Turing 1936
# tape model.
#
# === Recognition ancestry ===
#
# - Recognition #95 (@cascade candidate; Mara canonical
#   `ce4874b`, 2026-06-23): this species IS one of the cascade
#   species discharging the family-root.
# - Recognition #93 H4 RESOLVED (labeled<> functor at
#   `shards/labeled.mirror`): turing_artifact uses labeled<>
#   instance for program + translation metadata.
# - Recognition #51 (mirror as expanding Hilbert space): the
#   dimension-projection from LLVM IR's typed-SSA + optimization
#   surface to Turing tape's uniform-symbol surface is measurable
#   via `measure_llvm_turing`; the projection collapses many
#   basis vectors (types, registers, SIMD) into the tape's
#   single-symbol basis.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   Turing 1936               Alan Turing, "On Computable
#                             Numbers, with an Application to
#                             the Entscheidungsproblem", Proc.
#                             Lond. Math. Soc. s2-42:230-265.
#                             The tape-model this species
#                             targets.
#   Church 1936               Alonzo Church, "An Unsolvable
#                             Problem of Elementary Number
#                             Theory", Am. J. Math. 58:345-363.
#                             The λ-calculus / Turing equivalence
#                             grounding.
#   Alive2                    Lopes, Menendez, Nagarakatte, Regehr
#                             2021; LLVM translation-validation
#                             research. The empirical shape the
#                             per-instruction preservation lens
#                             references.
#   LLVM LangRef              LLVM Project; llvm.org/docs/
#                             LangRef.html. The source grammar
#                             this species measures against.
#   TCS translation           Standard textbook mapping in
#                             Sipser 2013 §3.1 (Turing machines
#                             simulate arbitrary computation).
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/polyglot-loss-aware-computational-
#               translation.md §4.1 + §4.2 Edge 2 + §9 M2 (Mara
#               `1ce68c3`, 2026-07-17 — the mint plan
#               forward-promise THIS shard discharges); §4.4
#               Edge 2 preservation/loss enumeration; §7.2
#               proof sketch grounding via Church-Turing.
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-lift-as-load-bearing]] (the
#                      lift is Church-Turing 1936 + Alive2 et al.
#                      translation-validation; NOT re-derived at
#                      substrate),
#                      [[feedback-loss-from-epistemologic-properties]]
#                      (loss is @epistemologic/properties composite,
#                      not Shannon, not invented),
#                      [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]] (every action
#                      body `\` blocked; FLOOR realisation domain).
# Related shards: shards/cascade.mirror (the family-root this
#                 specializes); shards/labeled.mirror (the functor
#                 primitive turing_artifact instance rests on);
#                 shards/code/llvm.mirror (source grammar; Mara
#                 M1 landed this session at `62d1b1c`);
#                 shards/code/turing.mirror (target grammar; Mara
#                 M1 landed this session at `7186410`);
#                 shards/cascade/code/rust/llvm.mirror (sibling
#                 mint this tick; composes with THIS species per
#                 polyglot spec §3.2 to give Rust → Turing);
#                 shards/cascade/code/turing/mirror.mirror
#                 (sibling mint this tick; composes with THIS
#                 species per polyglot spec §3.2 to give
#                 LLVM → mirror).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/cascade/code/llvm/turing.mirror` declares
# `@cascade/code/llvm/turing` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/programming-languages/llvm-langref
source @arxiv/theoretical-cs/turing-1936-computable-numbers

prism @cascade/code/llvm/turing {
  focus cascade
  project cascade
  split cascade
  shift cascade
  settle cascade
}

# === llvm_source carrier ===
#
# Specialization of @cascade.typed_source for source_grammar=llvm.
# References an `@code/llvm.llvm_ir_module` as the unit of cascade.
# The substrate re-declares this carrier as an alias for the
# module type so the cascade action signatures type-check at the
# species altitude; the underlying identity is the module's OID
# per @mirror/store discipline.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the module's content-addressed
# byte-form (LLVM IR text OR bitcode per LangRef §"Module
# Structure").
type llvm_source = llvm_ir_module

# === turing_translation_metadata carrier ===
#
# Structured carrier for the translation shape (SSA-to-tape-op
# encoding scheme, basic-block-to-state mapping, phi-node
# resolution strategy, symbol-alphabet choice, halt-state
# enumeration). Per [[feedback-no-bare-types]]: structured, not
# stringly. The carrier names load-bearing fields without fixing
# one translation scheme; the FLOOR resolver (Reed Tick M3)
# populates concrete values from its Rust-native implementation
# per Alive2-style per-instruction lowering.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type turing_translation_metadata = ref

# === turing_artifact carrier ===
#
# The @labeled<> instance per recognition #93 H4. A
# turing_artifact IS a `@code/turing.program` annotated with
# turing_translation_metadata via the labeled functor. Substrate-
# architecturally load-bearing: the program's typed identity is
# preserved (via labeled parametricity per Wadler 1989 / Reynolds
# 1983) while the translation-scheme dimension is added.
# `unlabel(artifact)` returns the program; `label_of(artifact)`
# returns the metadata.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the (program, metadata) pair
# (inherited from @labeled).
type turing_artifact = labeled(program, turing_translation_metadata)

# === apply_llvm_turing action ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING ACTION. Specialization of @cascade.compile for
# the LLVM IR → Turing tape functor. Takes an
# `@code/llvm.llvm_ir_module`; returns a `@code/turing.program`.
#
# Realisation: substrate-native LLVM IR → tape ops translation
# per polyglot spec §4.2 Edge 2 (each SSA instruction becomes a
# bounded tape-op sequence; each basic block becomes a state;
# each phi node becomes a branch). The FLOOR resolver (Reed
# Tick M3 under `[substrate-floor:@io-boundary]`) MUST discharge
# the body in Rust; THIS shard names the CONTRACT the FLOOR
# honors.
#
# Per Alex 2026-07-17 verbatim: the mapping is well-known (Alive2
# translation-validation research + Sipser 2013 §3.1 textbook
# construction); the FLOOR realizes it, the substrate names it.
#
# requires llvm_ir_valid(module): the source module MUST pass
# LLVM Verifier per `@code/llvm.llvm_ir_valid` (Mara `62d1b1c`).
# Ill-formed LLVM IR cannot be translated to tape ops; verifier-
# rejection halts the cascade.
#
# Body discharges at the FLOOR boundary.
apply_llvm_turing(module: llvm_ir_module, p: perturbation) -> program
requires llvm_ir_valid(module)
{ \ }

# === bundle_turing action ===
#
# Wraps a `@code/turing.program` + `turing_translation_metadata`
# into a `turing_artifact` via @labeled.label construction. The
# typed program gets the translation-scheme dimension added
# without losing the underlying program identity.
#
# requires turing_translation_coherent(program, metadata, p):
# bilateral commitment that the (program, metadata) pair coheres
# at the translation altitude — symbol alphabet matches program's
# transitions; state enumeration matches basic-block mapping;
# halt-state enumeration matches LLVM `ret`/`unreachable`
# derivation.
#
# Body discharges at the FLOOR boundary.
bundle_turing(prog: program, metadata: turing_translation_metadata, p: perturbation)
  -> turing_artifact
requires turing_translation_coherent(prog, metadata, p)
{ \ }

# === measure_llvm_turing action ===
#
# Specialization of @cascade.measure for the LLVM IR → Turing
# tape cascade. Returns substrate-typed measurement of information
# loss between llvm_ir_module's typed-SSA + optimization-annotation
# surface and turing_artifact's uniform-tape structure.
#
# Returns `imperfect<turing_artifact, ref, information_loss>` —
# the loss slot carries measured loss as substrate-typed data,
# NOT Shannon, NOT estimation; the composite of @epistemologic/
# properties per [[feedback-loss-from-epistemologic-properties]].
#
# The measurement IS substrate-architectural: read source's LLVM
# structure (register count, SIMD instruction count, memory-alias
# metadata density, optimization-attribute count, calling-
# convention annotations); read artifact's tape structure (state
# count, symbol alphabet size, transition count, halt-state
# enumeration); compute the dimension gap per polyglot spec §4.4
# Edge 2 preservation/loss enumeration.
#
# requires llvm_turing_loss_well_defined(module, artifact, p):
# bilateral that the measurement IS computable; the (module,
# artifact) pair must be a genuine cascade discharge.
#
# Body discharges at the FLOOR boundary.
measure_llvm_turing(module: llvm_ir_module, artifact: turing_artifact, p: perturbation)
  -> imperfect(turing_artifact, ref, information_loss)
requires llvm_turing_loss_well_defined(module, artifact, p)
{ \ }

# === turing_translation_coherent bilateral ===
#
# Target-side translation-well-formedness bilateral. Commitment
# that the (program, metadata) pair coheres at the LLVM-to-tape
# translation altitude.
#
# Splinter-pole: symbol alphabet finite and matches program's
# transitions; state enumeration matches basic-block mapping;
# halt-state enumeration derived correctly from LLVM `ret` /
# `unreachable` terminators; phi-node resolution strategy
# consistent across all basic blocks; program passes
# `@code/turing.turing_well_formed` (composes with Mara
# `7186410` bilateral).
# Narcissus-pole: alphabet drift; state mismatch; halt-state
# enumeration incomplete or over-approximated; phi resolution
# inconsistent; underlying program ill-formed per
# @code/turing.turing_well_formed.

bilateral turing_translation_coherent {
  sentinel "translation=symbol-state-halt-coherent"
  arity 2
}
turing_translation_coherent(prog: program, metadata: turing_translation_metadata, p: perturbation)
  -> verdict { \ }

# === llvm_turing_loss_well_defined bilateral ===
#
# Specializes the family-root's loss_well_defined for this
# cascade. Commitment that the substrate-typed gap calculation IS
# computable for the (module, artifact) pair; the module IS in
# @code/llvm grammar (verifier-passing), the artifact's program
# IS in @code/turing grammar (well-formed), and the pair
# represents a valid cascade discharge (`apply_llvm_turing`
# produced THIS artifact from THIS module).
#
# Splinter-pole: cascade-pair coherent; measurement well-defined;
# gap dimensions dischargeable per @epistemologic/properties
# composite.
# Narcissus-pole: source/artifact grammar mismatch OR pair does
# not represent a genuine cascade discharge; measurement
# undefined.

bilateral llvm_turing_loss_well_defined {
  sentinel "cascade=source-artifact-pair-discharge-witnessed"
  arity 2
}
llvm_turing_loss_well_defined(module: llvm_ir_module, artifact: turing_artifact, p: perturbation)
  -> verdict { \ }

# === cascade_llvm_turing_preserves_computation bilateral ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING composed bilateral for THIS species. Witnesses
# that the LLVM IR → Turing tape cascade preserves computational
# equivalence per Turing-completeness (Church-Turing 1936; Sipser
# 2013 §3.1).
#
# Per Alex 2026-07-17 verbatim ratification: the mapping is
# well-known; the cascade DOES lose LLVM optimization
# opportunities + register-level annotations + calling conventions
# + memory layout hints (all become uniform tape ops); it
# PRESERVES computational equivalence at the tape-model altitude
# per Turing-completeness of both LLVM IR and the tape machine.
#
# Splinter-pole: tape program computes the SAME function as the
# LLVM IR module per bisimulation up to bounded fuel (Milner
# 1989) OR per per-instruction Alive2-style translation
# validation; observable computational behaviour preserved.
# Narcissus-pole: cascade drifts computational semantics
# (translation-validation counterexample; bisimulation fails;
# tape program diverges where LLVM halts, or vice versa).
#
# Sentinel `cascade=preserves-tape-computation` per Mara
# `701828a` §1 byte-containment: content-addressed check on the
# cascade-pair OID vs the preservation-witness invariant. Rice-
# safe per Mara `701828a` — the CHECK is byte-level; the
# underlying question (full computational equivalence) is
# undecidable but the substrate discharges the sentinel-match
# at content-addressed altitude with bounded-fuel bisimulation
# per @code/turing's `equivalent` action shape (Mara `7186410`).

bilateral cascade_llvm_turing_preserves_computation {
  sentinel "cascade=preserves-tape-computation"
  arity 1
}
cascade_llvm_turing_preserves_computation(cascade_outcome: turing_artifact) -> verdict { \ }

# === llvm_turing_cascade_well_formed composed bilateral ===
#
# Specialization of @cascade.cascade_well_defined for this cascade
# instance. Composes the sub-predicates at this altitude per the
# landed cascade composed-bilateral shape.
#
# requires llvm_ir_valid(module): source LLVM IR module passes
# LLVM Verifier (composes with @code/llvm.llvm_ir_valid per Mara
# `62d1b1c`).
# requires turing_translation_coherent(unlabel(artifact, p),
# label_of(artifact, p), p): target-side translation well-formed;
# uses @labeled.unlabel + @labeled.label_of to extract program
# and metadata from the artifact.
# requires llvm_turing_loss_well_defined(module, artifact, p):
# loss measurement computable.
# requires cascade_llvm_turing_preserves_computation(artifact):
# computational-equivalence preservation witnessed at cascade
# altitude.
#
# All four must hold; substrate refuses cascade if source LLVM IR
# invalid OR translation incoherent OR loss undefined OR
# computation-preservation not witnessed.
#
# Splinter-pole: all four discharge; substrate-typed loss
# returned; cascade admissible per polyglot spec §5.3
# threshold gate.
# Narcissus-pole: at least one sub-predicate fails; cascade
# blocked; @fate re-selects per polyglot spec §6.

bilateral llvm_turing_cascade_well_formed {
  sentinel "cascade=all-sub-bilaterals-discharge"
  arity 2
}
llvm_turing_cascade_well_formed(module: llvm_ir_module, artifact: turing_artifact, p: perturbation)
  -> verdict
requires llvm_ir_valid(module)
requires turing_translation_coherent(unlabel(artifact, p), label_of(artifact, p), p)
requires llvm_turing_loss_well_defined(module, artifact, p)
requires cascade_llvm_turing_preserves_computation(artifact)
{ \ }

# === outbound declarations ===

out @cascade/code/llvm/turing
out llvm_source
out turing_translation_metadata
out turing_artifact
out apply_llvm_turing
out bundle_turing
out measure_llvm_turing
out turing_translation_coherent
out llvm_turing_loss_well_defined
out cascade_llvm_turing_preserves_computation
out llvm_turing_cascade_well_formed
